# Copper region sketch of the STM32H743 + SDRAM board (LAY-1, PWR-1, 3, 7, 8). Read by scripts/cu_sketch.py.
# This text is the source of truth for every pour; after a zone is dragged in KiCad it is read back
# into this file before anything else runs (PWR-7).
#
# Coordinates: mm from the board's top-left corner, x right, y down (board 85 x 75).
# State: stop 5 (power and copper), part A. The outer-layer regions hug the pads of their nets and are kept clear
# of the SDRAM line-order sketch (its L1 tracks east of the SDRAM run at x 61.6-62.6, y 37-46.3; nothing of +12V
# may go there). Current paths are at least 1.0 mm wide on the 12 V chain, the two buck outputs, +5V_BL and
# LED_A, and at least 2.0 mm on L3 (cu_sketch measure, build.sh copper). A through-hole pad a region touches is
# covered by pad + 0.5 mm or more, so its thermal relief (gap 0.254) keeps a ring of copper and no crumbs.
# Pads a region does not reach are tied by routes_power.py: QFN pins (0.5 mm pitch: a pour cannot pass between
# the neighbouring pins), the enable and feedback ends, pull-ups, and the vias to L3 and between L1 and L6.
#
# Floor plan (stop 4, see place.py):
#   top edge     headphone jack x 11-22, line-in jack x 23-34, SWD x 36-45, microSD x 47-63
#   left edge    RJ45 y 40-59, its body 4.1 mm over the edge (try/eth-west); PHY right of it at (22.4, 50.5);
#                QSPI flash under the MCU's SW corner (36, 58); user LEDs and key x 12-23, y 62-70
#   centre       MCU body x 35-45, y 32-42; SDRAM at (57, 37), body x 53-61, y 30.5-43.5; decoupling under both
#                BGAs on the bottom
#   right        CAN terminal on the right edge y 12-23 with the transceiver left of it; 3.3 V buck y 29-37;
#                5 V buck y 38-50; DC jack on the right edge y 52-64 with fuse, P-MOS, TVS and bulk left of it
#   bottom edge  LCD FPC x 28-54 (body front on the edge), debug UART x 56-67; backlight boost x 48-58, y 50-63
#   codec        under the jacks at (19, 26), LDOs north-east (3.3 V analog) and south (1.8 V) of it

origin 100 100
planes L2 L3 L5
gap 0.5                   # L3: distance between blocks of different nets (PWR-8)
clearance 0.2             # outer layers: local pour to anything else (user 2026-11-21, U33)
minwidth 0.2              # narrowest drawn part (user 2026-11-21, U33)

# ---- ground: L2 and L5 are whole planes, never cut; L1 and L6 are filled with ground where free
region L2_GND GND L2 whole
region L5_GND GND L5 whole
region L1_GND GND L1 whole minwidth=0.3
region L6_GND GND L6 whole minwidth=0.3

# ---- L3, the power plane. +3V3 is everything that is not one of the blocks below.
region L3_3V3 +3V3 L3 whole

# +5V: band down x 61.5-72 from the top strip to the 5 V buck output (R110) and its test pad, with an arm west
# under the backlight boost to its link R710 (x 51.3-64, y 48-55.5); the strip along the top (y 5.5-8.5, under the jacks, SWD and the
# microSD) runs to a leg at x 33.5-36.5 that comes down to the analog LDO link R112 (SPEC 5). Loads: U102 VIN
# and C108, R104 (EN pull-up), R814 (CAN 5 V link). A notch at y 20.8-24.4 leaves R813's +3V3 pad on +3V3 with
# room for its two vias. The strip and the leg are 3 mm wide: routes_power.py lets no via of another net cut them.
region L3_5V +5V L3
  33.5,5.5  72,5.5  72,20.8  67.2,20.8  67.2,24.4  72,24.4  72,52.3  64,52.3  64,55.5  51.3,55.5  51.3,48
  63,48  63,28  61.5,28  61.5,8.5  36.5,8.5  36.5,22.5  33.5,22.5

# +3V3A: under the codec, its analog decoupling and the LDO output (C111, TP104); a notch at x 24.4-27.6 keeps
# R610's +3V3 pad and its two vias on +3V3 (open to the south)
region L3_3V3A +3V3A L3
  8.6,17.8  30.6,17.8  30.6,24.7  27.6,24.7  27.6,21.6  24.4,21.6  24.4,31.9  8.6,31.9

# Block rails behind 0 ohm links (user 2026-11-20). The two BGA blocks are on L3 because their supply
# balls reach the plane through vias under the package (five blocks on L3, user 2026-11-21). Each reaches
# north in a tongue under the SDRAM bands to its link (R203, R301) and bulk capacitor (C217, C309), which sit
# above the bands; the tongue starts 0.5 mm east of the link's +3V3 pad.
# islands=remove (stop 5 part B): rings of dog-bone antipads box in crumbs of the block at ball positions, where no
# via can stand (a ball pad is above); KiCad drops them, the block itself is fed and kept.
region L3_3V3_MCU +3V3_MCU L3 islands=remove
  34,31  39.6,31  39.6,25  44.2,25  44.2,31  46,31  46,44.8  34,44.8
region L3_3V3_SDRAM +3V3_SDRAM L3 islands=remove
  52,29.5  55.6,29.5  55.6,25  61,25  61,29.5  62,29.5  62,44.5  52,44.5

# ---- outer-layer local pours. One or more per copper-class net of SPEC 5, around the placed pads.
# 12 V input chain, right edge, lower part: jack pin 1 and fuse; fuse to P-MOS drain
region L1_12V_JACK +12V_JACK L1
  67,58.9  69.45,58.9  69.45,57.15  73.15,57.15  73.15,60.85  67,60.85
region L1_12V_IN +12V_IN L1
  67.15,53.9  69,53.9  69,58.6  67.15,58.6
# +12V: from the 5 V buck input (C102, C104 across the VIN end of the package as in the LMR51420 layout example;
# both ground pads close the loop through vias, U56) down a column at x 65.55-67 between the feedback divider and
# the IC to C103 and TP101, a column at x 61.7-62.8 west of the zener past the P-MOS source, to the bulk
# capacitor C114 and across above it to the TVS D102. The SDRAM sketch's L1 tracks end at y 46.3, so the block
# round C103 starts at y 46.6. U101 pin 5 (EN, tied to +12V) is reached by a track (it sits between FB and BOOT).
region L1_12V +12V L1
  65.55,37.7  71.3,37.7  71.3,42.4  69.8,42.4  69.8,39.75  67,39.75
  67,52.1  62.8,52.1  62.8,54.95  66.95,54.95  66.95,56.7  62.8,56.7  62.8,61.05  72,61.05  72,67.2  69.5,67.2
  69.5,62.45  63.35,62.45  63.35,65.5  58,65.5  58,63.5  61.7,63.5  61.7,46.6  65.55,46.6
# 5 V buck: switch node kept small (pin 2 to the inductor; the bootstrap capacitor C101 by a track), output from
# the inductor to C105-C107 and down a 1.3 mm column at x 76.4-77.7 to C107 and the link R110 (R102, the feedback
# divider top, is reached by a track on L6 and two vias)
region L1_SW_5V SW_5V L1
  69.6,42.6  72,42.6  72,41.2  74.8,41.2  74.8,44.8  72,44.8  72,43.4  69.6,43.4
region L1_5V_REG +5V_REG L1
  77.8,40.3  84,40.3  84,44.5  80.8,44.5  80.8,45.5  77.7,45.5  77.7,50.1  72.75,50.1  72.75,47  76.4,47
  76.4,43  77.8,43
# 3.3 V buck (R105, the feedback divider top, is reached by a track on L6 and two vias); the output pour is
# chamfered below the inductor
region L1_SW_3V3 SW_3V3 L1
  70,31.05  72.4,31.05  72.4,30.2  74.5,30.2  74.5,32.7  72.4,32.7  72.4,31.85  70,31.85
region L1_3V3_REG +3V3_REG L1
  76.1,30.1  78.35,30.1  78.35,32.6  80.9,32.6  80.9,36  78.4,36  76.1,33.7
# LDOs beside the codec: analog 3.3 V input north-east of it, 1.8 V input and output south of it
region L1_5V_LDO +5V_LDO L1
  29.9,20.5  35.6,20.5  35.6,22  29.9,22
region L1_3V3_LDO +3V3_LDO L1
  14.1,30.1  19.65,30.1  19.65,31.15  17.6,31.15  17.6,31.5  14.1,31.5
# +1V8: LDO output, C603 / C113 / C604, and a strip between the ground pads to TP105; codec pin 32 by a short
# track (its neighbour pin 31 is CODEC_NRST, 0.5 mm away)
region L1_1V8 +1V8 L1
  20.4,29.1  23.1,29.1  23.1,30.3  27.5,30.3  27.5,32.5  25.7,32.5  25.7,30.8  23.8,30.8  23.8,33.8  22,33.8
  22,31.5  20.4,31.5
# codec IOVDD behind R610; pin 7 by a short track (pins 6 and 8 are 0.5 mm away)
region L1_3V3_AUD +3V3_AUD L1
  22.3,24.5  23.6,24.5  23.6,23.8  26.8,23.8  26.8,25.5  22.3,25.5
# MCU analog supply. The balls P1 / R1 sit in the MCU's south-west corner, which the SDRAM sketch closes on L1
# (FMC_A6), L4 (FMC_A10) and L6 (FMC_SDNWE): the filter and its capacitors are on the bottom under the corner
# (L6 pour) and the L1 pocket west of the balls (x 33.8-35.7, east of the HSE crystal's output track since
# stop 4 round 3). The two pockets overlap only inside the MCU rule area (L6: FMC_SDNWE runs down x 33.6 at the
# area's west edge; L1: FMC_A6 runs along y 43.5 below it): the dog-bone vias of P1 and R1 (part B of stop 5)
# join them. Part B moved C221, C223 and FB201 into the L6 corner bounded by FMC_SDNWE (x 33.6, y 45.6) and
# FMC_SDNRAS (x 38.375): the L6 pocket reaches down to y 43.5 over the VDDA pads of the two upright 1 uF
# capacitors, and an east lobe (x 36.55-37.2) takes the bead's VDDA pad, 0.2 mm below its +3V3_MCU pad.
region L1_VDDA_MCU VDDA_MCU L1
  33.8,40.6  35.7,40.6  35.7,41.85  34.9,41.85  34.9,43.2  33.8,43.2
region L6_VDDA_MCU VDDA_MCU L6
  34,40.95  36,40.95  36,42.85  37.2,42.85  37.2,43.7  36.55,43.7  36.55,43.5  34,43.5
# Ethernet PHY. VDDA_PHY: a column west of the PHY under the termination resistors and caps, with the two
# centre-tap pins of the RJ45 (through-hole, covered by pad + 0.5 mm all round) and C501 at its foot; PHY pin 19
# and C503 by short tracks, pin 1 by a track to C503. The bias resistor R505 moved to the bottom (under the PHY's
# south-west corner) to keep the column whole. FB501 sits east of the PHY next to +3V3_PHY: its VDDA side reaches
# the column by an L6 strip under the PHY's south side, widened at both ends for two vias each.
region L1_VDDA_PHY VDDA_PHY L1
  14.38,47.51  16.98,47.51  16.98,48.98  17.8,48.98  17.8,46  18.65,46  18.65,61.2  17.8,61.2  17.8,49.91
  16.98,49.91  16.98,50.11  14.44,50.11  14.44,51.38  11.84,51.38  11.84,48.78  14.38,48.78
region L6_VDDA_PHY VDDA_PHY L6
  17.7,55.95  28.9,55.95  28.9,58  26.9,58  26.9,56.95  18.7,56.95  18.7,58.6  17.7,58.6
# +3V3_PHY behind R514: C504, C505, FB501; PHY pin 9 and the MDIO pull-up R503 by short tracks (the pour reaches
# west to x 25.0 for them)
region L1_3V3_PHY +3V3_PHY L1
  25,50.6  26.5,50.6  26.5,51.45  27.9,51.45  27.9,53.2  31.1,53.2  31.1,55.4  27.3,55.4  27.3,53.3  25,53.3
# the remaining block rails
# QSPI: the flash is turned 180 degrees so VCC (pin 8) is at its south-west corner, out of the LCD fan; C401,
# C402, the link R404 and the IO3 pull-up R403 in a band west of it. The NCS and IO2 pull-ups R401 / R402 are on
# the bottom under the flash's east pin row (vias, stop 5).
region L1_3V3_QSPI +3V3_QSPI L1
  27.5,60.2  31.9,60.2  31.9,59.9  32.6,59.9  32.6,61.2  31.9,61.2  31.9,63.4  30.7,63.4  30.7,61.2  27.5,61.2
# LCD 3.3 V: link R709, C702, C701 in a column east of the LCD fan (x >= 47.8), straight down to connector pin 37
region L1_3V3_LCD +3V3_LCD L1
  48.4,60.2  49.85,60.2  49.85,68.6  49.4,68.6  49.4,69.6  49.1,69.6  49.1,68.1  48.4,68.1  48.4,67.65  49.3,67.65
  49.3,65.6  48.4,65.6  48.4,64.9  49.3,64.9  49.3,60.9  48.4,60.9
# microSD: link R812, C801, C802 in a band under the socket with a stub to contact 4, a strip between R802 and
# R803 down to a second band under the five pull-ups and the card-detect pull-up
region L1_3V3_SD +3V3_SD L1
  52.5,17.85  55.33,17.85  55.33,16.5  55.73,16.5  55.73,17.85  58.5,17.85  58.5,18.65  53.78,18.65
  53.78,21.5  58.9,21.5  58.9,22.5  51.1,22.5  51.1,21.5  53.42,21.5  53.42,18.65  52.5,18.65
# CAN: VIO (3.3 V) and VCC (5 V) of the transceiver behind R813 and R814 (the +5V_CAN column keeps 0.2 mm from
# C803's ground pad)
region L1_3V3_CAN +3V3_CAN L1
  69.2,18.5  70.2,18.5  70.2,23.2  69.2,23.2  69.2,21.4  68.2,21.4  68.2,20.8  69.2,20.8
region L1_5V_CAN +5V_CAN L1
  62.1,17.3  63.8,17.3  63.8,18  62.85,18  62.85,23.6  61.9,23.6  61.9,18  62.1,18
# backlight boost at the east end of the LCD connector (its pins 39 LED_A and 40 LED_K are the two easternmost;
# the link R710 takes +5V from the L3 arm). Switch node (L701 pin 2, U701 pin 1, D701 anode) >= 6 mm east of the
# easternmost straight LCD path (x 47.25); output capacitor C705 between the diode cathode and the IC's GND pin.
# +5V_BL: a 1.05 mm band from R710 above the inductor, east of C704's ground pad down to U701 pin 5 (C703 moved
# 0.4 mm north at stop 5 to keep the corner 1.0 mm wide).
region L1_5V_BL +5V_BL L1
  49.6,49.8  53.2,49.8  53.2,48.9  56.4,48.9  56.4,49.6  57.28,49.6  57.28,56.6  56.2,56.6  56.2,50.85
  51.35,50.85  51.35,53  49.6,53
region L1_SW_BL SW_BL L1
  53.1,51.5  54.2,51.5  54.2,55.45  55.35,55.45  55.35,56  53.2,56  53.2,58.5  52,58.5  52,55.45  53.1,55.45
# LED_A: diode cathode, C705, TP701, the dummy load R707 and a 1.0 mm strip down to connector pin 39; the last
# 1.1 mm narrows to the pin (0.35 mm between pins 38 and 40 at 0.5 mm pitch) and leaves pin 40 (LED_K) free to go
# north-east
region L1_LED_A LED_A L1
  50.075,59.9  56.2,59.9  56.2,58.1  58.4,58.1  58.4,61.2  56.2,61.2  56.2,62  54.4,62  54.4,64.5  53.1,64.5
  53.1,62  51.1,62  51.1,67.85  50.425,68.525  50.425,69.6  50.075,69.6
